From 1541e6d512e7011fe5658cbba4b246e178d37203 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: census fork spike <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:01:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Catch non-CFailure exceptions per function / per
 declaration group

The per-item handlers only caught CFailure. Any other exception (Failure from
ty_regions in the symbolic interpreter, Not_found from lookups of declarations
which failed to translate, in the pure micro-passes and in the extraction)
escaped and ended the run with no output and no indication of the item.

- Errors: exn_is_recoverable (everything but Out_of_memory / Sys.Break, and
  nothing when -abort-on-error is set) and save_uncaught_exn;
- Interp.evaluate_function_symbolic, Translate.translate_function_to_pure:
  an uncaught exception is reported against the function, like a CFailure;
- PureMicroPasses: the micro-passes are applied under a per-function handler;
  on failure the body is replaced with an error node (extracted as a hole),
  or the function is made opaque if that fails too;
- PureMicroPassesAnnots.add_type_annotations: same handler as for CFailure;
- Translate.extract_definitions: an uncaught exception in one declaration
  group no longer loses the file.

The two .borrow-check.out files change only in the source line of a warning.
